 60V  c  {+60}Ti produced in fragmentation of {+76}Ge{+30+} beam on a {+58}Ni   
 60V 2c  target.  LISE3 achromatic spectrometer used to separate fragments;     
 60V 3c  magnetic rigidity was tuned to optimize transmission of {+62}V         
 60V 4c  {+64}Cr fragments.  Transmitted nuclei were identified by three        
 60V 5c  consecutive Si detectors where two served for energy loss and          
 60V 6c  time-of-flight measurements while the last determined their residual   
 60V 7c  energies.                                                              
 60V  c  Measured E|g, I|g, I|b, |g|g, |b|g coin, |g(t), lifetimes with four Ge 
 60V 2c  detectors placed around a thick Si telescope.  Half-lives determined by
 60V 5c  fitting procedure involving five parameters: half-lives of mother,     
 60V 6c  daughter and grand-daughter nuclei, the |b-efficiency and the          
 60V 7c  background rate over the 1 s collecting time.                          
